From: CatPieLeaf <catpieleaf@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 20:30:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw89: fix RTW89_FW_CMD_OFLD_SRC_OTHER field overflow
 in delay ofld commands

GCC fails the build with:

    ./include/linux/bitfield.h:233:17: error: call to '__field_overflow'
    declared with attribute error: value doesn't fit into mask
      233 |                 __field_overflow();
    In function 'le32_encode_bits',
        inlined from 'rtw89_fw_cmd_ofld_enqueue' at fw.c:11586:12,
        inlined from 'rtw89_fw_cmd_ofld_udelay' at fw.c:11789:8
    (and again inlined from rtw89_fw_cmd_ofld_mdelay at fw.c:11803:8)

RTW89_H2C_CMD_OFLD_W0_SRC is a 2-bit wire field (GENMASK(1, 0), valid
range 0-3), but enum rtw89_fw_cmd_ofld_arg_src has five values:

    RTW89_FW_CMD_OFLD_SRC_BB       = 0
    RTW89_FW_CMD_OFLD_SRC_RF       = 1
    RTW89_FW_CMD_OFLD_SRC_MAC      = 2
    RTW89_FW_CMD_OFLD_SRC_RF_DDIE  = 3
    RTW89_FW_CMD_OFLD_SRC_OTHER    = 4   <- doesn't fit in 2 bits

rtw89_fw_cmd_ofld_udelay()/_mdelay() both build a DELAY-type command
with .src = RTW89_FW_CMD_OFLD_SRC_OTHER. GCC's inliner constant-folds
the whole call chain down to the enqueue function and proves the
resulting le32_encode_bits(4, GENMASK(1, 0)) call is out of range at
compile time, hence the hard error via __field_overflow's
attribute((error(...))). This does not reproduce with clang, which
apparently doesn't perform the same depth of interprocedural constant
propagation through the pointer-passed struct at the optimization
level in use here - the underlying overflow is real either way, just
silently truncated at runtime under clang instead of caught at
compile time.

Confirmed this is not kernel-p03-specific: current upstream
torvalds/linux master has the identical enum/GENMASK mismatch as of
this writing, so this is a latent, still-unfixed upstream bug that
just happens to get surfaced by GCC's stricter checking here.

rtw89_fw_cmd_ofld_enqueue()'s own validation only checks .src when
.type != RTW89_FW_CMD_OFLD_DELAY:

    if (cmd->type != RTW89_FW_CMD_OFLD_DELAY &&
        cmd->src != RTW89_FW_CMD_OFLD_SRC_RF &&
        cmd->src != RTW89_FW_CMD_OFLD_SRC_RF_DDIE &&
        !IS_ALIGNED(cmd->offset, 4))
            return -EFAULT;

confirming .src is a don't-care for DELAY-type commands - nothing in
this function or (by inference) the firmware side branches on its
value for that command type. Use RTW89_FW_CMD_OFLD_SRC_BB (0) instead
of SRC_OTHER in both delay helpers: it's in-range for the wire field
and behaviorally identical, since the value is never actually
consulted for DELAY commands.

Signed-off-by: CatPieLeaf <catpieleaf@proton.me>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/fw.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/fw.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/fw.c
@@ -11779,8 +11779,17 @@

 static void rtw89_fw_cmd_ofld_udelay(struct rtw89_dev *rtwdev, u32 us)
 {
+	/*
+	 * .src is a don't-care for DELAY-type ofld commands (see the
+	 * early-out in rtw89_fw_cmd_ofld_enqueue(), which only validates
+	 * .src when .type != RTW89_FW_CMD_OFLD_DELAY), but it still gets
+	 * encoded into the wire word via RTW89_H2C_CMD_OFLD_W0_SRC, a
+	 * 2-bit field (GENMASK(1, 0)). RTW89_FW_CMD_OFLD_SRC_OTHER is enum
+	 * value 4 and doesn't fit - use SRC_BB (0), any in-range value
+	 * works identically here.
+	 */
 	struct rtw89_fw_cmd_ofld_arg cmd = {
-		.src = RTW89_FW_CMD_OFLD_SRC_OTHER,
+		.src = RTW89_FW_CMD_OFLD_SRC_BB,
 		.type = RTW89_FW_CMD_OFLD_DELAY,
 		.value = us,
 	};
@@ -11793,8 +11802,9 @@

 static void rtw89_fw_cmd_ofld_mdelay(struct rtw89_dev *rtwdev, u32 ms)
 {
+	/* See rtw89_fw_cmd_ofld_udelay() comment. */
 	struct rtw89_fw_cmd_ofld_arg cmd = {
-		.src = RTW89_FW_CMD_OFLD_SRC_OTHER,
+		.src = RTW89_FW_CMD_OFLD_SRC_BB,
 		.type = RTW89_FW_CMD_OFLD_DELAY,
 		.value = ms * 1000,
 	};
